// ── Punctuation is never vocabulary or grammar ──────────────────────────────
// The grammar gate flags any segment typed 'grammar' whose surface is not a
// declared form. Punctuation reaching it as a grammar segment therefore produced
// "untaught grammar particle: 。". Several segmenters skip only the FULLWIDTH forms,
// so an ASCII '?' or '.' from the model fell through as an unclassified character.
const JA_PUNCT_RX = /^[\s\u3000\u3001\u3002\u30FB\uFF1F\uFF01\uFF0C\uFF0E\u2026\u2015\u301C.,!?;:'"()\[\]\-\u2018\u2019\u201C\u201D]+$/
